# Repo-root .dockerignore — applies to the Docker build context for
# api/Dockerfile when render.yaml's `dockerfilePath: ./api/Dockerfile` is used
# without rootDir (build context = repo root).
#
# The Dockerfile only `COPY`s three top-level paths (api/, data-schema/,
# source-texts/parsed/), so anything outside those is already excluded from
# the image. This file mainly keeps the build context Docker uploads to the
# daemon small — faster builds, less log noise.

# Python / build artifacts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Local secrets — never ship a real .env into an image
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
*.pem
*.key

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Local scratch — Yoshi's workspaces, not for the image
_scratch/
_inbox/

# Source trees that the Dockerfile does not COPY (kept out of build context
# for build-speed reasons — already not in the image regardless).
# Exception (S112): the tiered commentary loader at
# restoration-pipeline/_session112_load_matthew_tiered_commentary.py IS
# copied into the image so it can be run from Render Shell. Negate the
# broad restoration-pipeline/ exclusion at file granularity: exclude all
# immediate children of restoration-pipeline/, then re-include the loader
# files we ship.
# Exception (S114): the partner-tier reconciliation script also ships in
# the image — same Render-Shell-from-the-API-service pattern.
# Exception (S117): the multi-mark migration loader ships in the image.
# Exception (S120): the Strong's data ingestion loaders ship in the image
# AND the source-texts/kjv + source-texts/strongs-{hebrew,greek} directories
# they read are also un-excluded so the loaders have their inputs at runtime.
# Exception (S124): the Bookmarks + Notes V1 migration loader ships in the
# image. Forward-fix lesson — this .dockerignore allow-list must update
# alongside every Dockerfile COPY for a new loader, OR the COPY matches
# zero files and Docker silently no-ops. Three-artifacts-in-lockstep
# (SQL + loader + Dockerfile COPY) becomes FOUR: + .dockerignore negate.
restoration-pipeline/*
!restoration-pipeline/_session112_load_matthew_tiered_commentary.py
!restoration-pipeline/_session114_reconcile_partner_tiers.py
!restoration-pipeline/_session117_apply_multi_mark_migration.py
!restoration-pipeline/_session120_load_strong_entries.py
!restoration-pipeline/_session120_load_verse_words.py
!restoration-pipeline/_session124_apply_bookmarks_and_notes_v1.py
!restoration-pipeline/_session197c_run_remaining.py
!restoration-pipeline/_session199_apply_overlay.py
source-texts/existing-restored-editions/
source-texts/extras/
commentary/
app/

# Project tracking / docs (not runtime)
BIBLE_APP_ROADMAP.md

# Git internals
.git/
.gitignore

# Old api/.dockerignore — leftover from the rootDir:api design; not used now
# that the build context is the repo root, but kept in the repo for history.
